<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acarnania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Acarnania is a region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambracian-gulf">Ambracian Gulf</a>, the Achelous river and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a>. In antiquity its people, the Acarnanians, lived in small towns joined in a federal league centred on Stratos, and they were long allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> against Corinth's colonies and later with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolians">Aetolians</a>. It is now part of the regional unit of Aetolia-Acarnania.</p></div>
